{"study_accession":"PRJNA708208","secondary_study_accession":"SRP309931","title":"Transcriptional profiling of human KIR+ and KIR- CD8 T cells by bulk RNA-seq","description":"Previous reports show that Ly49+CD8+ T cells can suppress autoimmunity in mouse models of autoimmune diseases. Here we find a markedly increased frequency of CD8+ T cells expressing inhibitory Killer cell Immunoglobulin like Receptors (KIR), the human equivalents of the Ly49 family, in the blood and inflamed tissues of various human autoimmune diseases. Moreover, KIR+CD8+ T cells can efficiently eliminate pathogenic gliadin-specific CD4+ T cells from Celiac disease (CeD) patients’ leukocytes in vitro. Furthermore, we observe elevated levels of KIR+CD8+ T cells, but not CD4+ regulatory T cells, in COVID-19 and influenza-infected patients, and correlate with disease severity and vasculitis in COVID-19. Expanded KIR+CD8+ T cells from these different diseases display shared phenotypes and similar T cell receptor sequences. These results characterize a regulatory CD8+ T cell subset in humans, broadly active in both autoimmune and infectious diseases, which we hypothesize functions to control self-reactive or otherwise pathogenic T cells. Overall design: KIR+ and KIR- CD8 T cells (CD3+CD56-CD8+) were sorted from healthy subjects (N=5), MS (N=3), SLE (N=4) or CeD (N=1) patients and then subjected to RNA-seq analysis. CD8 T cells with high or low expression of KIR2DL3 or KIR3DL1 were sorted from the blood of healthy subjects (N=3) and subjected to RNA-seq analysis.","pubmed":"35258337","geo_series":"","n_samples":38,"study_labels":[{"level":"study","event_code":"ACUTE_VIRAL_INFECTION","certainty":"confirmed","delta_days":null,"delta_bucket":"UNK","time_precision":"unknown","stage":"teacher","confidence":1.0,"evidence":"Furthermore, we observe elevated levels of KIR+CD8+ T cells, but not CD4+ regulatory T cells, in COVID-19 and influenza-infected patients, and correlate with disease severity and vasculitis in COVID-19.","model_version":"teacher:mlx:mlx-community/Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct-4bit"},{"level":"study","event_code":"AUTOIMMUNE_FLARE","certainty":"ruled_out","delta_days":null,"delta_bucket":"UNK","time_precision":"unknown","stage":"teacher","confidence":1.0,"evidence":"Furthermore, we observe elevated levels of KIR+CD8+ T cells, but not CD4+ regulatory T cells, in COVID-19 and influenza-infected patients, and correlate with disease severity and vasculitis in COVID-19.","model_version":"teacher:mlx:mlx-community/Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct-4bit"}],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN18221338","study_accession":"PRJNA708208","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"HC2_KIR+","description":"HC2_KIR+","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM5145525","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2022-03-12","attributes":[["source_name","healthy_KIR+ CD8 T"],["subject status","healthy"],["tissue","PBMC"],["cell_type","KIR+ CD8 T"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR13911656","experiment_accession":"SRX10291294","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 4000","read_count":50417889,"base_count":7663519128,"first_public":"2022-03-12","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 4000 sequencing: GSM5145525: HC2_KIR+ Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN18221339","study_accession":"PRJNA708208","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"MS3_KIR-","description":"MS3_KIR-","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM5145524","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2022-03-12","attributes":[["source_name","multiple sclerosis_KIR- CD8 T"],["subject status","multiple sclerosis"],["tissue","PBMC"],["cell_type","KIR- CD8 T"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR13911655","experiment_accession":"SRX10291293","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 4000","read_count":44346380,"base_count":6740649760,"first_public":"2022-03-12","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 4